  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14214505/assets/6613de40d3150985d471d97fd3b5369cd67df2ae248b22ce99af011f3484a20c.png)\n\nThe function $g(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-5,3].$ The graph of ${g}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $g(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5,$ $4,$ and $7$ respectively (from left to right). Find the maximum value of $g(x)$ on the interval $[-5,3]$ given that $g(-2)=3.$\n\n${g}_{\\text{max}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
